    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T15:02:17Z",
    "body": "Decision (maintainer, 2026-11-13, in chat): \"then that is the decision, workflow_dispatch\".\n\n- The PR test workflow has a `workflow_dispatch` trigger only (input: the PR number). No `pull_request`, `push` or `schedule` trigger.\n- It is started by the review skill / PR-reviewer agent of a collaborator's session after the diff has been read (`gh workflow run pr-test.yml -f pr=<N>`, then `gh run watch`); the review comment carries the run's link and result. A fork PR cannot start a run by itself.\n- The workflow file runs from main, so it checks out the PR head itself (`refs/pull/<N>/head`), trial-merges it with main, and runs with a read-only token and no secrets.\n- PRs that are \"read, not built\" today (a new dependency, a `build.rs` / scripts / `.github` change) are not sent to the runner.\n- No runner online, or the run is cancelled or times out: the review builds locally as today, or reports \"not built\"; never a pass.\n\nThe other open questions in the issue body (Windows-only readings, concurrency, UI suites) stay open.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
